      "content": "Ibuprofen, even in standard over-the-counter doses such as 400mg, can interact with other medications (like elixium) and may affect underlying health conditions. Its safety relies on individual circumstances, including your full medical history and overall health. A single 400mg dose might seem low, but without professional advice, this can't be clearly defined as safe, especially without knowing about your heart conditions and your body's reactions. I urge you to consult with a healthcare provider as soon as possible or consider alternative temporary pain relief methods. Safety is paramount when it comes to managing health.",
